-- title:
--   Riemann–Roch space of the weight-2m floor divisor
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $N\ge 1$ and $m$ a natural number, and let $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the series $q$-rescalings `qExpand K d (jqModC K)` for the divisors $d\mid N$, $d\ge 1$; here `jqModC K` is the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$ with coefficients reduced into $K$, and $j$ denotes it viewed as an element of $F$. Assume $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the subfield $K(j)$ generated by $j$. Let $D$ be a divisor of $F/K$, i.e. a finitely supported integer-valued function on the places of $F$ over $K$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $K$, distinct from $F$, whose local ring is a principal ideal ring), and suppose that for every place $w$, with $\mathrm{ord}_w$ the associated normalised valuation, $$D(w)=\big[\mathrm{ord}_w j>0\big]\,\tfrac{2m\,\mathrm{ord}_w j}{3}+\big[\mathrm{ord}_w(j-1728)>0\big]\,\tfrac{m\,\mathrm{ord}_w(j-1728)}{2}+\big[\mathrm{ord}_w j<0\big]\,m\,\mathrm{ord}_w j,$$ the two fractions being integer quotients, hence floors since their numerators are non-negative. Let $G\in F$ lie in the Riemann–Roch space of $D$, i.e. $\mathrm{ord}_v G\ge -D(v)$ at every place $v$. Then `IsModPFormFn K m G` holds for the Laurent series underlying $G$: the product $G^6 j^{4m}(j-1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra of $K((q))$ generated by `jqModC K`, and $G^2 j^m(j-1728)^m$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by `jqModC K`$^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the inclusion of the Riemann–Roch space $L(D_{2m})$ of the weight-$2m$ floor divisor into the space of weight-$2m$ holomorphic functions described by the two integrality conditions of `IsModPFormFn`; combined with the opposite inclusion it identifies the two spaces, and in particular exhibits the integrality-defined space as a $K$-vector space of finite dimension. It is used in the construction of mod-$p$ cusp forms and in the production of Hecke eigenvectors from eigenvectors in Riemann–Roch spaces.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isModPFormFn_of_mem_riemannRochSpace.lean

